                  "status": "Open",
                  "severity": "Medium",
                  "type": "Tampering",
                  "description": "See OWASP Automated Threat #6:\nUsing speed to violate explicit or implicit assumptions about the application’s normal use to achieve unfair individual gain\n\nPersonal explanation: This is Medium severity because it is accessible to the user through the account login form, creating a public facing attack surface.",
                  "mitigation": "Defences include providing enforcement of behavioural workflow and anti-automation. \n\nPersonal explanation:  The above can work because it can prevent external threats from misusing the public facing service from being attacked with speed.",
